 because the taliban although they have  said they respect women's rights  we really haven't seen much of that so  uh  i think the gains we have made in health  care in education uh  those are all been uh  i wouldn't say totally destroyed but uh  they're likely to totally be lost  john sopko the special inspector general  for afghanistan reconstruction thank you  so much for being with us here tonight  it's a pleasure to be here thank you  up next this week's winners and losers  in the media see if you agree with the  choices made by the editors of mediaite  you're watching brian ross investigates  on the law and crime trial network  time now for this week's winners and  losers in the media as chosen by the  editors of mediaite and we're joined by  aidan mclaughlin who's the  editor-in-chief of mediaite which like  the law and crime trial network is part  of the dan abrams media group and aiden  was chosen as your winner of this week  brian kilmeade of fox who broke ranks  and actually called president trump a  liar let's look at this  right now nobody cares about 2020 nobody  and everything that he said and the  challenges that he made should have been  done before the election and they did a  recount in arizona and the recount  showed no difference almost and he came  out and said it showed that they won  arizona that's an outright lie  and please stop wasting our time with  that because he's capable of doing so  much more  well what do you make of that aidan  well so this is part of an ongoing  effort on behalf of a lot of trump's  media supporters to convince the former  president to stop spreading lies about  the 2020 election and move on to  subjects that americans actually care  about uh brian kilmeade who is the host  of fox and friends trump's favorite  morning show said there on his radio  show that the 2020 election is not a  priority for many americans despite the  fact that trump keeps bringing it up in  his rallies and in his statements to  supporters um that's all fair but that  comment that you played right there that  kill me made which is calling specific  claims that trump has made about the  2020 election calling them outright lies  that's really notable and that stands  out against previous comments that other  trump supporters have made um i should  note that it also contrasts a lot with  what other hosts at fox news have said  about this um i spoke to uh pete  heggseth  a top fox news host recently and i asked  him if he could tell me who won the 2020  election and he could not answer that  question so there are still many hosts  out there that are struggling with that  question on fox news and in right-wing  media um we wanted to give brian  kilmeade kudos for being clear-eyed  about it and saying we know that the  2020 election was won by joe biden  donald trump challenged this in the  courts the courts including ones uh  which were run by uh trump trump  appointed judges threw all these  challenges out we know who won the 2020  election let's move on  in this case though brian kilmeade said  this on radio not on his tv show  right and i do think that that's notable  um brian kilmeade's radio show obviously  has a much smaller audience uh than fox  and friends which is the show that he  hosts for three hours every day  now he has in the past in the past  couple of years when trump was president  after trump left office occasionally  challenged the president um so i will  give him props for that but it is  notable that he's saying this on his  radio show and not on fox and friends  let's move on now to the loser this week  james bennett formerly of the new york  times who ran the new york times opinion  page why is he a loser  so james bennett who until recently was  the top editor of the opinion pages of  the new york times took stand in a trial  uh over an opinion piece the paper  published a few years ago um he left the  uh paper uh recently you'll remember  over a backlash over an opinion piece  that was published by tom cotton calling  for the military to be brought in to  handle protesters uh over the killing of  george floyd um this trial is about a  different opinion piece um that the new  york times published it was published by  the editorial board and it claimed that  the shooting of then congresswoman gabby  giffords was incited by an ad  run by sarah palin's super pac um james  bennett who was part of the editorial  board at the time inserted that line  establishing that link at the last  minute now there was no link between  those two events and the times had to  correct the story the next day uh now  sarah palin is suing the paper for  defamation um and james bennett uh said  in testimony that he takes full  responsibility for that line being added  um he said that the pressing deadline of  the paper going to print was what made  him hastily add that line that ended up  being incorrect um but it resulted in  this major lawsuit and a huge headache  for the new york times  obviously mistakes happen for major  publications like the new york times but  this was a serious one that has resulted  in a lawsuit now  that threatens to challenge the first  amendment protections that the paper has  in this case though he did not blame  some lower level researcher or deputy  and took full responsibility and issued  a correction the next day  i think that's admirable that he took  full responsibility but it's still a  serious error to establish this link of  inciting violence between uh sarah  palin's super pac  and the horrible tragedy that happened  um the you know the good news for the  new york times is that uh the press  enjoys pretty pretty good protections um  against defamation lawsuits uh sarah  palin and her lawyers will have to prove  that they acted with actual malice and  knew what they were printing was  incorrect  and did so regardless which is a really  hard thing to prove and is part of the  reason why the new york times has not  lost one of these defamation lawsuits in  decades  so this is a lawsuit being closely  followed by everybody in the media and  libel lawyers to see how it comes out  sarah palin versus the new york times  it'll be a big verdict when it comes aid  mclaughlin thank you so much for being  with us here tonight  thanks brian and thanks to all of you  for joining us this evening and thanks  to our great staff here at long crime  for guinea is on the air and off the air  every single week  [Music]  so  you
 

